From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: domicile CI <ci@domicile.invalid>
Date: Tue, 17 Nov 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] domicile: Mesa's drivers load before the GPU sandbox

A card the browser hands the GPU process after its sandbox is up opens
Mesa's GBM backend inside the sandbox. The loader then looks up each
library the backend links by path through the broker, which refuses
those outside Mesa's directories. On NixOS each library is in its own
store path, so LLVM was refused and the card showed only software
output (#2225):

  MESA-LOADER: failed to open dri: libLLVM.so.21.1: cannot open shared
  object file: Permission denied

LoadDomicileMesaDrivers loads every `*_gbm.so` and `*_dri.so` in Mesa's
directories (beside libgbm, /run/opengl-driver/lib, GBM_BACKENDS_PATH,
LIBGL_DRIVERS_PATH) before the sandbox, as Chromium does for AMD on
ChromeOS. Inside the sandbox the loader finds the linked libraries
already loaded, by name. A driver that does not load logs the loader's
reason as an error, such as a glibc it needs that the engine lacks.

Verified: not built. This repository cannot build Chromium; the engine
job builds it on `crux`.
---
 content/common/gpu_pre_sandbox_hook_linux.cc | 133 +++++++++++++++----
 1 file changed, 104 insertions(+), 29 deletions(-)

